spans.s:
1. स्फारित, अस्, आ, अम् (for 2. see p. 1152), made
to quiver or vibrate [cf. वि-स्फारित]; throbbing;
vibrating.

), to cause to grow large, enlarge,
augment, increase; [cf. Gr. σπά-ω, σπά-σ-μα, σπα-σ-μό-ς,
ἀ-σπάζομαι, ἀγαπάω (i. e. ἀγαν-σπαω);
Lat. spa-ti-um, patere; Old Germ. spannan, spa-
nan; Angl. Sax. spanan, spinnan; Goth. spin-
nan.]
